"""Portlin first-boot setup wizard.

Runs once on tty1 before the display manager, and gives the stick its identity:
account, hostname, locale, keyboard, timezone, and optionally a new LUKS
passphrase so the person holding the stick owns the key rather than whoever
built it.

Deliberately stdlib-only and whiptail-driven rather than graphical. This runs
before X on hardware nobody has tested, where a text UI on tty1 is the only
thing guaranteed to work.
"""

